    "top_frame": "Tied through six innings until the offense found eight runs in one inning.",
    "what_this_means": "Houser gave them a clean foundation. Six innings, one run allowed, and the bullpen locked it down behind him. But what separated this from a close game was the eighth: Arraez walked to spark a rally that turned a manageable lead into a rout. The lineup had been waiting for that moment, and when it came, they finished it. This is what a stabilizing trend looks like. Pitching that holds firm enough for late offense to matter, and an offense patient enough to capitalize when the window opens. They were never behind, never panicked, and never wasted the opportunity once the game broke open.",
